Names that collide with the first word of a word operator.

`starts` is the plural of the `start` inspector *and* the first word of
`starts with`; likewise `ends`, and `does` for the `does not ...` family.
A phrase ends at one of these only when the trie matches the operator in
full, so the reading is decided by what follows, never by the word alone.

(Everything above the first ==== is ignored by the loader. Do not put notes
*between* records -- they would be read as part of the previous expected tree.)

==== a plural inspector name that is also an operator's first word
starts of ranges of current system intervals of power histories
----
(of (ref "starts")
  (of (ref "ranges")
    (of (ref "current system intervals") (ref "power histories"))))

==== a multi-word name ending in `starts`
date range starts of bes actions
----
(of (ref "date range starts") (ref "bes actions"))

==== a multi-word name ending in `ends`
stop on idle ends of task settings
----
(of (ref "stop on idle ends") (ref "task settings"))

==== a colliding name is an ordinary comparison operand
date range starts of bes actions is greater than now
----
(bin "is greater than"
  (of (ref "date range starts") (ref "bes actions"))
  (ref "now"))

==== exists takes a colliding name as its operand
exists starts of ranges
----
(exists (of (ref "starts") (ref "ranges")))

==== not exists takes a colliding name as its operand
not exists starts of it
----
(not-exists (of (ref "starts") it))

==== aggregation over a colliding name
number of starts of it
----
(number-of (of (ref "starts") it))

==== a colliding name filters like any other collection
exists starts whose (it > now)
----
(exists (whose (ref "starts") (bin ">" it (ref "now"))))

==== the real-world clause this fix was written for
exists (now - it) whose(it > 8 * hour) of starts of ranges of current system intervals whose(idle state = state of it) of power histories
----
(exists
  (of
    (whose (bin "-" (ref "now") it) (bin ">" it (bin "*" (num "8") (ref "hour"))))
    (of (ref "starts")
      (of (ref "ranges")
        (of
          (whose (ref "current system intervals")
            (bin "=" (ref "idle state") (of (ref "state") it)))
          (ref "power histories"))))))

==== `starts with` wins when the name could have absorbed `starts`
starts starts with "a"
----
(bin "starts with" (ref "starts") (str "a"))

==== `ends with` wins even when the phrase itself ends in `ends`
date range ends ends with "z"
----
(bin "ends with" (ref "date range ends") (str "z"))

==== the operator wins on both sides at once
starts of it starts with starts of it
----
(bin "starts with" (of (ref "starts") it) (of (ref "starts") it))

==== `does not start with` still matches in full over a colliding name
starts of it does not start with "a"
----
(bin "does not start with" (of (ref "starts") it) (str "a"))

==== a cast target still stops at a real operator
x as string starts with "a"
----
(bin "starts with" (cast (ref "x") "string") (str "a"))

==== a partial `does not ...` is still an error, at the structural word
x does not start of it
----
ERROR line 1 column 8

==== a dangling operator word after a non-reference operand is still an error
it ends "a"
----
ERROR line 1 column 4

==== a dangling operator word after a parenthesized operand is still an error
(x) ends "a"
----
ERROR line 1 column 5
